---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How UtilityBox handles data: what runs in your browser, what our server sees, and how Google AdSense works on this site."
>
  <div class="container privacy-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        UtilityBox is a collection of free calculators and utility tools. Every calculation — the scientific
        calculator, unit converter, UK salary calculator, network calculator, word tools, and generators — runs
        entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Nothing you type into those tools is sent to our server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What happens on this site right now</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't require accounts, logins, or any personal information to use any tool.</li>
        <li>
          We don't run our own analytics and don't set any cookies ourselves. We do use Google AdSense to show
          ads, and Google's ad script sets cookies of its own — see "Advertising" below.
        </li>
        <li>
          Our web hosting provider's server automatically records standard access logs for every request
          (IP address, page requested, referrer, user agent, and timestamp), the same as almost any website.
          These logs are used only to keep the site running, debug problems, and detect abuse — we don't
          analyse them for marketing purposes or share them with third parties.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Third-party requests</h2>
      <p>Three tools on this site talk to an external service in order to work:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Currency Converter</strong> — fetches exchange rates from the
          <a href="https://www.frankfurter.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Frankfurter API</a>
          (European Central Bank data). Your device makes this request directly, so your IP address is visible
          to that service the same way it would be to any site you visit. We don't send it any of your other
          data. See the <a href="https://www.frankfurter.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Frankfurter</a> project for their terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>DNS Lookup</strong> — sends the domain name (and record type) you enter directly from your
          browser to <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/1.1.1.1/encryption/dns-over-https/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's public DNS-over-HTTPS resolver</a>
          to fetch the results. Nothing passes through our server. See
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for their terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Word Unscrambler / Word Builder</strong> — download a static word list from our own server.
          No data is sent, only received.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>No other tool on this site makes any network request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site shows ads served by <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. To do that, every page loads a script
        from Google (<code>pagead2.googlesyndication.com</code>). Google may set cookies and use information
        about your device and browsing activity to choose which ads to show you, including personalized ads
        based on your interests, unless you've opted out or restricted this.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're in the UK, EEA, or Switzerland, you'll see a consent prompt (powered by Google's Funding
        Choices) before any personalization happens. The choice you make there controls whether Google shows
        you personalized or non-personalized ads on this site — you can change your answer at any time by
        clearing your cookies and reloading the page, which brings the prompt back.
      </p>
      <p>You can:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Manage or turn off ad personalization</a> directly with Google.</li>
        <li><a href="https://myaccount.google.com/data-and-privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review your wider Google privacy settings</a>.</li>
        <li>Use a browser or extension that blocks third-party ad cookies or scripts.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We don't control what Google does with the data its ad script collects — see
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>
        and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>
        for that. We still don't run any analytics of our own, and we don't sell or share data with anyone
        beyond what's needed for Google to serve ads.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because we don't collect personal data beyond standard server logs, there is very little of yours for us
        to hold. If you're in the UK or EU (GDPR) or California (CCPA) and have questions about what our server
        logs contain or want something removed, contact us using the details below and we'll do our best to help.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change what data this site collects — most likely by adding ads or analytics — we'll update this
        page and the "Last updated" date above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy? Email <strong>privacy@utilitybox.wales</strong>.</p>
      <p><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  section ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  section p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  section li {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  section code {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
